Aw, dude, that's awesome.

13:17.936 --> 13:18.935
All right, good night, kiddo.

13:18.979 --> 13:20.304
I'm gonna go hide out
in the dry tub

13:20.357 --> 13:21.610
And watch your sister
take a wizz.

13:28.335 --> 13:30.297
Dad, thanks again
for filling in

13:30.341 --> 13:32.510
After chris got
all big-headed and quit.

13:32.553 --> 13:34.849
I'm excited to start shooting
these videos with you.

13:34.893 --> 13:36.395
Yeah, um, about the videos--

13:36.397 --> 13:38.149
I couldn't help but notice

13:38.193 --> 13:40.738
You've got me squatting
on generic jell-o,

13:40.782 --> 13:41.991
Not the name brand.

13:42.034 --> 13:43.327
Does it make a difference?

13:43.371 --> 13:45.874
[laughs]
doe-does it make a difference?

13:45.918 --> 13:47.505
You're-you're adorable.

13:47.549 --> 13:50.302
And why am I snorting
regular cocaine

13:50.304 --> 13:53.102
When I specifically requested
bacon-wrapped cocaine?

13:53.104 --> 13:55.315
There's no such thing
as bacon-wrapped cocaine.

13:55.317 --> 13:57.696
Yeah, tell that
to chris farley's autopsy photo.

13:57.740 --> 13:59.911
Also, your nose
is bleeding heavily.

14:00.956 --> 14:03.502
Yeah, that's allergies. I'm
allergic to bacon and cocaine.

14:03.546 --> 14:06.176
I tell you, this is the most
unprofessional film set

14:06.178 --> 14:08.931
<i>Since they cast
timothée chalamet in dune.</i>

14:08.975 --> 14:11.857
My father came, not for spice,

14:11.901 --> 14:13.944
Not for riches--

14:13.988 --> 14:15.908
-Whoa-- wh-whoa!
-Cut.

14:15.951 --> 14:17.661
-Wind guy.
-I told you guys

14:17.705 --> 14:19.791
He shouldn't
be in windy movies.

14:19.834 --> 14:21.796
Freakin' told you guys.

14:24.640 --> 14:26.475
All right,
we've got just one week

14:26.519 --> 14:29.732
To turn you into a normal,
regular kid who can be adopted.

14:29.776 --> 14:32.363
Parents love reading a-b-c books
with their little ones,

14:32.406 --> 14:34.409
So let's practice that,
shall we?

14:35.581 --> 14:37.836
A, asswipe.

14:37.879 --> 14:40.216
Okay, close, close.
How about this one?

14:40.260 --> 14:42.011
B, bastard.

14:42.055 --> 14:43.474
We are oh-for-two.

14:43.518 --> 14:44.768
Yeah, I'm gonna skip c.

14:44.854 --> 14:46.648
Feel like I know what
you're gonna say for that.

14:46.692 --> 14:50.116
<i>D, f. And I know
you're gonna go for that f.</i>

14:50.118 --> 14:51.326
Not the usual f.

14:51.370 --> 14:53.456
Yeah, I'm not sure
this is gonna work.

14:57.301 --> 14:58.678
You're, like,
two hours late, dad.

14:58.680 --> 15:00.473
I'm sorry meg,
but as an artist,

15:00.475 --> 15:02.229
I simply cannot create

15:02.273 --> 15:03.481
Until you are finished
dry cleaning

15:03.525 --> 15:06.363
-All of my Halloween costumes.
-I tried,

15:06.407 --> 15:08.117
But they couldn't
get the stain out of your

15:08.161 --> 15:09.536
Emperor palpatine robe.

15:09.538 --> 15:12.921
Take it someplace else.
Take it everyplace else.

15:12.923 --> 15:14.173
Ugh.

15:14.217 --> 15:16.179
♪

15:16.223 --> 15:19.354
<i>♪ we keep doing montages ♪</i>

15:20.190 --> 15:23.029
<i>♪ about the wrong things ♪</i>

15:23.073 --> 15:25.785
<i>♪ here's another one
 we should have cut ♪</i>

15:25.787 --> 15:28.793
<i>♪ but the guy
 who draws these up ♪</i>

15:28.836 --> 15:32.718
<i>♪ and lost custody
 of his kids ♪</i>

15:32.762 --> 15:35.224
<i>♪ he got a dui ♪</i>

15:35.268 --> 15:38.857
<i>♪ since the last montage. ♪</i>

15:40.448 --> 15:42.702
[chris sighs]

15:45.459 --> 15:48.507
Chris, what are you doing?
[sniffs]

15:48.551 --> 15:50.511
Why does it smell
so bad in here?

15:50.555 --> 15:53.477
Uh, well, my exotic pets

15:53.521 --> 15:55.274
Somehow all killed each other.

15:56.571 --> 16:00.452
Still not quite sure
what the sequence was there.

16:00.495 --> 16:03.167
Anyway, meg, I just want to say
I'm really happy

16:03.169 --> 16:06.801
For you and dad that you're
doing that website together.

16:06.845 --> 16:08.847
Uh, thanks, chris.

16:08.849 --> 16:10.477
No, thank you.

16:10.520 --> 16:13.232
I just wish I didn't
screw everything up, you know?

16:13.234 --> 16:15.071
Treated you like a carrot muffin

16:15.114 --> 16:16.699
I butt-smothered for money.

16:16.743 --> 16:19.374
But you're not a carrot muffin,
you're my sister.

16:19.417 --> 16:20.667
And I forgot that.

16:20.711 --> 16:23.509
It's okay, chris,
I forgive you.

16:23.552 --> 16:26.182
Hey, call out
any boston market sides.

16:26.226 --> 16:29.105
It's Friday, and we're gorgin'.

16:31.739 --> 16:33.741
♪

16:35.748 --> 16:40.090
Told you, stewie, nobody
wants to adopt this loser.

16:43.852 --> 16:44.894
Okay, look sharp.

16:44.938 --> 16:46.564
These people
may be your last chance.

16:46.607 --> 16:49.613
Just do everything
the way we rehearsed it.

16:49.657 --> 16:51.911
Hey, little man, how are you?

16:51.955 --> 16:54.541
I am fine
and in good physical health.

16:54.585 --> 16:57.800
Aw. What kind of toys
do you like, sweetie?

16:57.844 --> 17:00.474
Um, you know, a doll,
because that's okay

17:00.476 --> 17:01.601
For a boy, I'm told.

17:01.644 --> 17:03.313
But, you know,
any-any toy's fine.

17:03.356 --> 17:04.900
An outside ball
for throwing inside.

17:04.902 --> 17:06.321
I mean, you know,
whatever you got.

17:06.364 --> 17:08.660
So sweet. Hey,

17:08.704 --> 17:10.289
What do you want to be
when you grow up?

17:10.333 --> 17:11.500
When I grow up, I want to be

17:11.543 --> 17:13.964
A body-cam-off police officer.

17:14.008 --> 17:16.596
I-I mean, just a regular
police officer.

17:22.487 --> 17:25.276
How would you
like us to adopt you

17:25.286 --> 17:26.828
So that you can
come live with us

17:26.872 --> 17:29.753
And be a jets fan,
not a pats fan,

17:29.797 --> 17:32.091
Because we are a jets family.

17:32.928 --> 17:35.225
[exclaiming]

17:35.269 --> 17:38.607
[bleep] jets are a straight
[bleep] [bleep] franchise, bro.

17:38.651 --> 17:40.736
The last jet that actually
mattered in nyc

17:40.780 --> 17:42.284
Is the one that
hit the south tower.

17:42.327 --> 17:43.828
Whoa, whoa.

17:43.871 --> 17:46.752
Okay, so that wasn't a match.

17:51.223 --> 17:53.685
I'm sorry. I really thought
I could help you find

17:53.729 --> 17:55.230
A family of your own.

17:55.232 --> 17:56.735
What's going on over there?

17:56.820 --> 17:59.784
Holy crap, it's mark wahlberg's
seven freckle-chested sisters

17:59.828 --> 18:00.870
<i>From the fighter.</i>

18:00.913 --> 18:03.960
I'm sorry, ladies,
you have to leave.

18:04.004 --> 18:05.548
What? For why?

18:05.591 --> 18:08.137
We caught you
sneaking outside beers

18:08.181 --> 18:09.515
Into the adoption fair.

18:09.517 --> 18:11.814
If you're going to be
at the adoption fair

18:11.857 --> 18:14.611
You have to buy
adoption fair beers.

18:14.613 --> 18:16.699
Fine, we'll drink
in the parking lot.

18:16.701 --> 18:18.578
Whatever kid doesn't get picked,

18:18.580 --> 18:20.458
Just leave him outside.

18:20.460 --> 18:22.672
Hey, April, check out that one.

18:22.715 --> 18:24.594
Whoa, now that's a good-looking

18:24.638 --> 18:27.392
Government subsidy right there.

18:27.435 --> 18:30.900
-Um, hi there.
-Hey, bud.

18:30.944 --> 18:34.576
I see you got the same
aaron hernandez tattoo I got.

18:34.620 --> 18:36.749
Want to come live with us?
We live near an overpass

18:36.793 --> 18:39.337
And we got lots and lots
of d batteries to throw.

18:43.057 --> 18:45.353
Go on, get out of here.

18:48.486 --> 18:50.532
Have a great life
with your seven moms.

18:50.576 --> 18:52.244
Well, one of 'em will be my mom.

18:52.288 --> 18:53.999
Six of 'em
will be my girlfriend.

18:54.042 --> 18:56.713
[short chuckle]
the dude's a legend.

19:03.315 --> 19:06.404
Hey, baby. I want to party
with that ice cream cone.

19:06.447 --> 19:08.700
Five bucks and I'll sit on it.

19:10.541 --> 19:11.875
Hey. Hey.

19:13.254 --> 19:16.553
Twenty bucks if you'll mash
a chipwich with your knee.

19:16.598 --> 19:18.225
[sighs]

19:18.268 --> 19:19.937
Let's see the chipwich.

19:19.939 --> 19:22.610
No! He doesn't do knee stuff.

19:22.654 --> 19:24.865
What is wrong with you sickos?

19:24.909 --> 19:26.620
What happened to you, man?

19:26.664 --> 19:28.541
This is all I'm good for, meg.

19:28.585 --> 19:30.839
It's... It's all
people see me as.

19:30.882 --> 19:32.759
That's not true, chris.

19:32.803 --> 19:34.429
You have so much to offer,

19:34.473 --> 19:37.103
And I've got something
for you.

19:37.146 --> 19:38.438
Buttercream?

19:38.482 --> 19:41.113
You bet your ass, buttercream.

19:42.117 --> 19:43.452
Wait.

19:43.496 --> 19:45.708
This one we do together.

19:47.464 --> 19:49.466
[laughing]

19:49.510 --> 19:51.639
["love life us up where we
belong" by joe cocker
& jennifer warnes playing]

19:51.641 --> 19:55.900
<i>♪ love lift us up
 where we belong ♪</i>

19:57.487 --> 19:59.741
<i>♪ where the eagles cry. ♪</i>

20:06.051 --> 20:08.639
So, chris,
after your recent adventure

20:08.682 --> 20:11.227
Behind the scenes
of the adult video world,

20:11.271 --> 20:13.943
You're probably not even
able to enjoy pornography any--

20:14.028 --> 20:15.821
Wrong!

20:15.865 --> 20:18.621
Uh, okay.
Well, I got to go to

20:18.706 --> 20:19.874
The county registrar's office.

20:19.917 --> 20:22.003
Need to re-register
our business as inactive

20:22.047 --> 20:23.967
And change our filing status.

20:23.969 --> 20:24.969
♪

20:25.012 --> 20:27.851
<i>♪ undoing a corporation ♪</i>

20:27.853 --> 20:31.611
<i>♪ is surprisingly complicated ♪</i>

20:31.655 --> 20:33.908
<i>♪ but it still doesn't make ♪</i>

20:33.952 --> 20:37.541
<i>♪ for a good montage. ♪</i>

20:37.584 --> 20:40.089
Hey, gavin.
Yeah, it's dad.

20:40.133 --> 20:43.222
Well, the court say I get
two guaranteed calls a week,

20:43.266 --> 20:45.894
So I'm calling.
[chuckles]

20:45.938 --> 20:49.153
Can you please tell your mother
to get off the extension?

20:49.197 --> 20:52.201
No, in-person visits
have to be supervised,

20:52.245 --> 20:54.625
But the calls do not
have to be supervised,

20:54.669 --> 20:57.173
So she can
get off the phone now.

20:57.216 --> 21:00.806
Daddy knows what mommy's
breathing sounds like, bud.

21:00.808 --> 21:03.021
Get off the phone, janet!